  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q:review-venue-skew",
      "question": "How much of this map is an artifact of review-site selection bias? Trustpilot and Capterra are where people go when something broke or when a vendor asked them to post; Reddit and private accountant communities were not reachable during this pass.",
      "why": "Nine of eleven pains lean on review-site verbatims. Support responsiveness in particular could be badly over-weighted relative to how the median customer experiences it.",
      "would_change": "If neutral community voice shows support as a minority complaint, pain:no-one-to-call drops from high to medium confidence and pain:new-state-registration, which is corroborated by independent forum discussion, becomes the strongest pain in the map."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:micro-multistate",
      "question": "Do under-10 owners actually hit the multi-state registration pain, or is it concentrated in the 10-100 remote-hiring segment?",
      "why": "The strongest multi-state verbatims come from founders hiring distributed teams, not from local businesses with one location. The segment assignment on pain:new-state-registration is currently an inference.",
      "would_change": "If it is a 10-100 pain only, it stops being a wedge for the micro segment and the micro story should lead on tax filing correctness and payday reliability instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:accountant-switching-trigger",
      "question": "What actually makes an accountant move a whole book of clients, versus complaining and staying?",
      "why": "Two accountants in the sources say they moved everything, but both cite a single account-level incident. It is unclear whether that is the real trigger or the last straw after unrecorded friction.",
      "would_change": "If the trigger is cumulative rather than a single incident, the accountant segment needs a retention and early-warning story, not an incident-prevention story."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:time-tracking-evidence",
      "question": "Is pain:hours-and-pto-dont-flow real at scale, or is it three unlucky reviews?",
      "why": "It rests on three sources, one of them from 2018, and it is the only pain where the underlying job (getting hours into a pay run) is barely discussed in public at all.",
      "would_change": "If more evidence does not surface, this pain should be cut or demoted to latent, since silence may mean it is genuinely solved rather than unspoken."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:employee-voice-channel",
      "question": "Where do employees talk about payroll when nothing has gone wrong?",
      "why": "Every employee verbatim found is a complaint about a late or missing deposit. That biases the employee pain toward reliability and hides whatever else they care about, such as pay transparency, withholding accuracy, or mobile access.",
      "would_change": "A second employee pain could emerge, which matters because employees are the largest user population and the least represented in this map."
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    { "id": "src:1", "url": "https://gusto.com", "title": "Gusto", "venue": "Company website", "speaker": "seller", "published": null, "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Payroll, benefits and HR for small businesses, run by 500,000+ businesses." },
    { "id": "src:2", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Theodore Hoss, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-14", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I have almost no confidence that Gusto is filing the taxes properly because I get emails warning of errors, for example, that our L&I risk class codes are incorrect and they may not be able to file properly as a result. Except when I check our information, it is all correct and updated. The upshot is I have been having to file L&I taxes myself, which kind of makes me pissed about paying every month for gusto to NOT do their job." },
    { "id": "src:3", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Scott McQuade, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-12", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Try getting someone knowledgeable on the phone. Good luck. And when you finally reach someone, communication can be extremely difficult, and instead of getting your problem solved, prepare yourself for more questions than an FBI profiler interrogating a suspected serial killer. ... I left Paychex because I thought their service was terrible. Gusto somehow managed to make me appreciate Paychex. I didn't think that was possible. ... Bigfoot has been spotted more often than Gusto customer support." },
    { "id": "src:4", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Diane, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "customer", "published": "2026-08-14", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "My paycheck is late and they say there is nothing wrong, but it will be deposited by 7 PM CT. Seriously?! Chatted with a rep who had a nonchalant attitude and said we never guarantee the checks will be deposited first thing in the morning. Yeah, when every other paycheck was deposited by midnight without fail and now all of the sudden, its not there, that causes US so many issues." },
    { "id": "src:5", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Howie Dewitt, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-14", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "1 star is too many. Worst payroll company on earth! Payroll was submitted days ago. Its 2:30 pm on payday, still no deposits. They may even hold the money until Monday. How do they get away with being this terrible?" },
    { "id": "src:6", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Carolyn Silvey, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-04", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "We were with Gusto for 11 years. Last week, we were told by Gusto there was a tax issue and account had been suspended. We contacted state and determined there was no problem. Gusto said they would work as quickly as they could to reinstate our account. 2 hours before we are set to run payroll, we get an email that they have cancelled our account. No warning, no explanation, and will not take my calls. I had to figure out paychecks for 76 people, write out checks, fedex checks to 3 states and make loans to staff who could not get checks in bank. I never would have believed this could happen." },
    { "id": "src:7", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Jess, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-10", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "At the time of cancellation, I was told that my services would be discontinued. However, approximately three months later, I discovered that money was still being withdrawn from my bank account for the 401(k) service. I was then informed that the 401(k) was handled as a separate service or entity and apparently had not been discontinued along with my other Gusto services. ... I would strongly caution other small business owners to make sure they understand every separate service connected to their Gusto account, who actually provides that service, how much it costs, and exactly what must be done to cancel each service individually." },
    { "id": "src:8", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Veronica Borges, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-08-06", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I was promised a callback from a supervisor multiple times and it never came. Every representative I spoke with had no real visibility into my case and no authority to actually resolve anything!! At one point I had to compile my own complete case timeline myself and send it to Gusto's own 'support staff', because nobody there had reviewed the case before responding to me." },
    { "id": "src:9", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Rick Leibowitz, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-08-05", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I have had three clients on the system and ran into a glitch with one. I dealt with customer service on two occasions and gave them a second chance when a payroll failed to direct deposit funds on time for our employees (never a good situation for a company). ... when I cancelled after not being able to process the payroll on July 31st and had to switch to another payroll provider, they charged me for a full month of service in August that I have not received." },
    { "id": "src:10", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Kathryn, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-08-04", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Spoke with 5 customer service agents over the course of 1.5 hours and no one was able to help me understand my account balance (many numbers were incorrectly given). I asked to speak to a manager or supervisor and no one was available. Nothing was resolved in over 1.5 hours and I missed 2 other important meetings. My daughter pediatric bill has still not been paid. Considering moving our company benefits to someone else." },
    { "id": "src:11", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Angela Richards, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-12", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "DO NOT USE GUSTO!! They do not acknowledge ANY of your own company forms to save to employee files. They force you to use their forms even though those forms dont work for your state. They will not run your payroll until you complete their forms.This is a lawsuit waiting to happen." },
    { "id": "src:12", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Austin Arnold, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-31", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Can't make payments to an employee. Every single pay period I spend half a day with AI chatbots, horrible UX, and roundabout solves just to pay one employee." },
    { "id": "src:13", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Duncan St Croix, 2-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-19", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "When payroll issues came up, it was difficult to get timely, useful support, and we felt like we were left without clear ownership or resolution. Payroll problems are time-sensitive and affect employees directly, so slow or unclear support creates real operational stress for a business. We expected better communication, clearer escalation, and faster help." },
    { "id": "src:14", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Aaron Griver, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "customer", "published": "2026-08-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "They dont help employees. If an employer doesnt pay and payroll bounces they dont leave it to show it. Instead delete it and say 'We cant see it since it wasnt run'. Even though it was ran it just bounced" },
    { "id": "src:15", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Wade Wall, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-19", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "It is clear that their customer support system is set up as a firewall to ensure actual employees never have to interact with dissatisfied clients. The support reps function strictly as a go-between, passing messages back and forth without any real authority to fix the company's bad service." },
    { "id": "src:16", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "R R, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-04", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "They botched the first payroll 3 times. I ended up going to a different service provider. I was told on a recorded line that I would not be charged but I was charged, and then charged AGAIN for the next month. It then took 3 hours on the phone and on a chat to get 1 of the 2 months refunded." },
    { "id": "src:17", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=2", "title": "Lori, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-12", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "The onboarding process was a nightmare and it has just declined since then. It is impossible to be able to talk to a manager when you try to get things resolved." },
    { "id": "src:18", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Gwen, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "customer", "published": "2026-09-17", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Their customer service is awful and once you are no longing using them they hold your W2s" },
    { "id": "src:19", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Anne, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-09", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "The employee was given the 2014 version of the state W4 form (it's 2026)" },
    { "id": "src:20", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Ben Hall, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-09", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "we cannot get a real response out of them...going on 3 weeks. I still have no answers." },
    { "id": "src:21", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Chris Clark, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-17", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Overpromised, repeated benefits errors, and painfully slow resolution" },
    { "id": "src:22", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Mariana Navarrete, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "customer", "published": "2026-09-17", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "BEEN WAITING ON A PAYMENT FOR 10+ DAYS, IT SAYS CONFIRMED BUT ITS NOT IN MY ACCOUNT" },
    { "id": "src:23", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com", "title": "Thomas Harris, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-03", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "THEY KEEP BILLING YOU $260/MONTH...charged me over $500!!!" },
    { "id": "src:24", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=4", "title": "Mark, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-01", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Gusto cancelled my employees' dental and vision insurance without telling me...Gusto is a danger to your business." },
    { "id": "src:25", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=4", "title": "Jennifer Tendero, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-01", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Two different Gusto agents told us in writing that payroll was reversed and would not be deposited. It was deposited anyway." },
    { "id": "src:26", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=4", "title": "Eric M., 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-06-29", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "The support is AI...chat with techs who know less about the software than most users." },
    { "id": "src:27", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=6", "title": "Stephanie McCollum, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-04-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I never had an issue with Gusto until my employees W-2 came back incorrect and they handled so unprofessionally. I consulted an IRS agent as well as a tax professional that determined that Gusto support was incorrect and giving me the wrong information..." },
    { "id": "src:28", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=6", "title": "Dee Smith, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "customer", "published": "2026-04-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "As an employee I have to say Gusto is the worst payroll service ever. Payday is today. In every single job I've had since direct deposit was born, you wake up and your money is in your account. With gusto, it can be hours or all day..." },
    { "id": "src:29", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?page=6", "title": "Stephanie Emmons, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-04-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Even if you pay for the dedicated representative, they don't respond to you for weeks, if ever. They have messed up our payroll on more than one occasion, removed pay after submission of numbers, wiped out our PTO..." },
    { "id": "src:30", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=state", "title": "Robin Agricola, 2-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-06-10", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Where Gusto gets 5 stars is with the basics of running payroll. Very easy, have never had an issue. However, with compliance issues...0 stars. I had two employees move from Utah to Massachusetts in September 2025. The transition between states was not managed properly by Gusto, and I ended up in a SEVEN MONTH LONG battle with the state to transfer their wages. I tried to lean on Gusto throughout this process, and they basically just kept saying, 'Just wait, it takes time for the wage transfer request to get filed.' Well, seven months later, I'm now EXTRA behind on what the state thinks I owe them, and Gusto is just like, 'This issue has already been resolved.' Excuse me, but no. Nothing was resolved. I ended up just paying the $1,000 fee to get the state off my back. Gusto really screwed the pooch on this one, and now I have NO confidence in their ability to keep me compliant." },
    { "id": "src:31", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=state", "title": "EY, 2-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2025-11-19", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "They withheld $$'s from our bank but didn't file the State quarterly until 5 months later, resulting in thousands of $'s in penalties to us." },
    { "id": "src:32", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=state", "title": "TLM, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2025-12-08", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Arizona DES requires quarterly reports even if no wages were paid" },
    { "id": "src:33", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=clients", "title": "Angel, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-06-30", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Gusto billed me $184 with no advance notice, and when I disputed it, their support couldn't even locate my own account. I'm a CPA who runs payroll for client businesses on Gusto - every one of those clients came in through my referrals. ... read the billing terms closely and test their support before you commit." },
    { "id": "src:34", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=clients", "title": "Scott, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2023-07-08", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I had my account locked out. I have hundreds of clients I work with and because a single one didn't pay their bill, I am locked out of ALL the accounts I'm linked to. ... Accountants beware, this is NOT the company for you." },
    { "id": "src:35", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=clients", "title": "Vernon L Kury, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-04-14", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I have removed all of my clients from Gusto's platform and will not be returning. Trust is critical in payroll services." },
    { "id": "src:36", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "Colleen McNally, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2021-02-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "It took over $1000 in CPA fees before Gusto admitted this costly error... pay the extra fee now with ADP or Paychex or pay later...in the thousands." },
    { "id": "src:37", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "Dan Pittenger, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2021-04-22", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I ended up paying my accountant $250 to fix a mistake on Gusto's end.", "unused": "Corroborates pain:tax-filed-wrong but adds nothing the stronger 2026 verbatims do not already carry; kept for provenance." },
    { "id": "src:38", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "Broc Curry, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2024-06-25", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "After this situation I had my accountant look closer and she pointed out that Gusto was incorrectly filing state taxes." },
    { "id": "src:39", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "Sophon Meas, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-03-24", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I am in a nightmare scenario with Gusto... their accounting system is automatically charging me another $5,428.40 and an additional $9K in form 940/941 according to my local accountant." },
    { "id": "src:40", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "MN, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2024-05-29", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "hiring an accountant would be worth the price given how much agony calling in every week caused.", "unused": "Supports pain:no-one-to-call but is two years older than the verbatims already carrying it." },
    { "id": "src:41", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=accountant", "title": "Vic, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2023-10-12", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "their Philippines-based support team gave me incorrect information that could have gotten me in BIG trouble with the IRS if my accountant hadn't fixed it." },
    { "id": "src:42", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/gusto.com?search=time+tracking", "title": "Mark, 1-star review of Gusto", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-06-18", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Gusto has a broken PTO system that cannot be fixed. Updating a paid time off policy automatically cancels the unpaid time off policy. ... This is a platform bug that has been open and unresolved for months. I have spent more than 15 hours on hold or in calls with support agents..." },
    { "id": "src:43", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28729562", "title": "codegeek comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I run one of those companies and hence speaking from experience. I want to hire employees (not contractors) all over the United States but it is such a pain." },
    { "id": "src:44", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28729562", "title": "codegeek comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I did that in 2 states already (in addition to primary state) and drowning with shitty paperwork." },
    { "id": "src:45", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28729562", "title": "rahimnathwani comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "When you hire an employee in a new state, you usually have to do these things differently: 1. State income and payroll taxes 2. State unemployment insurance 3. Workers compensation insurance" },
    { "id": "src:46", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28730050", "title": "stevesearer comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "operator", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "We use Gusto for payroll but have to spend a not-insignificant amount of time wrestling with each state's system." },
    { "id": "src:47", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28729562", "title": "codegeek comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I want a federal law in the United States that allows you to hire anyone in any state without doing the 'Register in my state' bullshit." },
    { "id": "src:48", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=19902542", "title": "codegeek comment on health insurance costs", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2019-05-13", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I run a small business and it costs about $2000/Month group premium for a family of 4...So give or take, $25K per year per family/employee." },
    { "id": "src:49", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20104094", "title": "BrentOzar comment on small business health insurance", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2019-06-05", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "health insurance companies make that massively complicated, with various rules about where the majority of staff lived, where each person lived, which plans were available" },
    { "id": "src:50", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=929842", "title": "tptacek comment on offering health benefits at a startup", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2009-11-08", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "For the first year or so of our company, we didn't offer health benefits, and that cost us candidates...The current system distorts both the health care market and the job market" },
    { "id": "src:51", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=9745540", "title": "waterlesscloud comment on small business payroll taxes", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2015-06-20", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I've lost count of how many times I've heard of owners of small businesses keeping payroll taxes, getting caught, and cutting a deal with the IRS to stay out of prison that means they have to sell the business RIGHT NOW" },
    { "id": "src:52", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=17804993", "title": "MattRogish comment on payroll compliance and PEOs", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2018-08-20", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Getting this wrong can destroy your company, and PEOs are super cheap by comparison!" },
    { "id": "src:53", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28729562", "title": "tomrod comment on 'CEOs are at their wits' end'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2021-10-02", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "You typically need a business license for a state where you have employees and...there are typically legal and other costs." },
    { "id": "src:54", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=8080442", "title": "matthewmacleod comment on running a small business", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "founder", "published": "2014-07-24", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "I can't stress enough (at least from having run a small business) that accounting is the number one thing to get correct from the get-go. It saves such an immense amount of time, money and stress later on." },
    { "id": "src:55", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=50", "title": "People Operations Coordinator, Apparel & Fashion, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2018-08", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "A bit glitchy when importing hours sometimes Doesn't automatically payout Ca meal break violations" },
    { "id": "src:56", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=2", "title": "SHANNON H., Insurance Team Lead, Medical Practice, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-08-13", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "run payroll as often as needed without extra charges ... new hires enter their own information ... customer support is only during weekday hours. There is no weekend availability" },
    { "id": "src:57", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=3", "title": "Tiffany A., VP and Head of Employee Success, Computer Software, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2025-10-15", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Overall, it was fine when we were a small sized company. As we got closer to 50+ is when the problems began. ... I don't like the customer service, it's an email and it can takes an extended amount of time to get any issues resolved." },
    { "id": "src:58", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=3", "title": "James L., Consultant, Accounting, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2025-12-20", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "The benefits management portion of Gusto dropped the ball in a pretty significant way." },
    { "id": "src:59", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=2", "title": "Carlie R., Owner, Arts and Crafts, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-03-03", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "system ran a little bit slower ... paychecks were going out late" },
    { "id": "src:60", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/131882/Gusto/reviews/?page=2", "title": "Verified Reviewer, Office Manager, Construction, Gusto review", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-01-07", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Works really well and is easy to navigate. The onboarding and benefits are streamlined ... customer service can be a little frustrating at times" },
    { "id": "src:61", "url": "https://www.healthsystemtracker.org/brief/how-much-and-why-premiums-are-going-up-for-small-businesses-in-2027/", "title": "How much and why premiums are going up for small businesses in 2027", "venue": "Peterson-KFF Health System Tracker", "speaker": "analyst", "published": "2026-08-06", "pulled": "2026-09-17", "verbatim": "Median premium increase of 14% (25th percentile 10%, 75th percentile 18%); 59% of small group market insurers are raising rates between 10-20%; the median insurer estimate of the underlying increase in the cost of healthcare is 10.8%." }
  ]
}
